the State Department has told a key  figure in president Trump's Ukraine  lobbying effort not to answer questions  from Congress today as scheduled  Gordon Sandlin the US ambassador to the  European Union had agreed to speak with  House impeachment investigators Nancy  Cordes is on Capitol Hill so Nancy he  said he would speak and now he's not  showing up what does this mean for  future witnesses well what it means  Democrats fear is that other state  Department officials who have been  scheduled to be deposed won't show up  either this cancellation took everyone  by surprise  Soglin himself had flown in from  Brussels for this deposition and  according to his lawyer quote early this  morning the u.s. Department of State  directed ambassador Sandlin not to  appear today for his scheduled  transcribed interview the lawyer says  ambassador Sunland is very disappointed  that he won't be able to testify and  that he hopes this is cleared up soon so  that he can but Democrats are already  citing this as another instance of  obstruction of justice by this  administration they want to talk to  Sandlin because he was pushing the  president's priorities in Ukraine harder  than just about anyone namely priorities  that included investigations into the  2016 election and into the energy  company that hunter Biden worked for in  one text message Sandlin insisted that  there was no quid pro quo that's what  Democrats had wanted to ask him about  today well Nancy that certainly is a  plot twist who else does the committee  want to hear from well most notably they  want to hear from the one and now  possibly two whistleblowers who have  come forward they've been engaged in  conversations with the whistleblowers  lawyer trying to get security clearances  lined up so that they can conduct this  closed-door interview however the  President and other Republicans have  said so frequently that they want to be  able to confront this whistleblower  perhaps have him testify publicly the  president says he wants to meet his  accuser that Democrats say they're now  considering extraordinary measures to  conceal this whistleblowers identity  when he does go before  Congress they say they're thinking about  obscuring his face or his voice or  altering them perhaps having him testify  remotely because they're so concerned  that his not anonymity will be blown  Nancy thank you very much
 

